<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aetolian League</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th–2nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aetolian League was a federation of the cities and tribes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aetolia">Aetolia</a> in west-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> that became a leading power in the third century BCE. It dominated Delphi and the Amphictyony after defending the sanctuary against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauls">Gauls</a> in 279 BCE. First an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, it then sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> and after its defeat in 189 BCE became a subordinate ally of Rome.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aetolian-league.jpg" alt="Aetolian League" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ca:User:Jolle · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Etolia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
